## Exp53 — Nearest-Edge M5 Impulse Timing Family — FAIL

Exp53 was the final preregistered historical timing-feature family before the fresh-forward gate.

Scientific question: does the local closed-M5 impulse at state_time, oriented toward the nearest fixed corridor boundary, add a robust EXIT-vs-NO_EXIT clock component beyond BASE_EXIT?

Frozen causal features:
- nearest boundary = BACK when |close-back| <= |forward-close|, otherwise FORWARD.
- EDGE_BODY_ATR = edge_sign * (M5_close - M5_open) / ATR.
- BAR_RANGE_ATR = (M5_high - M5_low) / ATR.
- EDGE_CLOSE_LOC = edge_sign * (2*M5_close - M5_high - M5_low)/(M5_high-M5_low), clipped [-1,1], zero for zero-range bars.

Implementation note before score: the initial runner aborted because dyn does not itself carry raw M5 close/ATR. No Exp53 score had been accepted. The runner was corrected to causally map unique closed-M5 open/high/low/close/ATR to state_time with many-to-one state mapping and explicit cardinality guards. The scientific contract did not change.

All mapping/environment guards PASS: 9667 states mapped; M5 timestamp universe 99999; state cardinality preserved; all eight EXIT environments scorable.

TRAIN diagnostics: feature rank 3/3; standardized condition number 2.793005; JOINT3 design rank 27/27; converged=True; finite=True. EXP53_JOINT3_IDENTIFIABILITY=PASS.

