### Diagnostic interpretation — preserved, not a rescue

The local M5 impulse family is NOT a universal EXIT clock. However, it is not classified as useless. Point gains were positive in many environments and BODY_EXIT showed multiplicity-adjusted evidence in TEST_EARLY_DOWN (Holm p=0.0048 for both Brier and LogLoss). RANGE_EXIT also changed sign by environment, including clear degradation in VALIDATION_EARLY_UP. AUCs for JOINT3 were generally only modestly above 0.5. Therefore the correct historical classification is NON-UNIVERSAL / REGIME-CANDIDATE, not ROBUST and not DISCARDED.

No marginal, drop-one, horizon subset, environment subset or event-day exclusion may rescue Exp53 after the result.

