## Next phase — prospective Market Operability layer, not historical rescue

The next scientific phase is NOT another historical timing experiment. A separate Market Operability layer may be designed prospectively before fresh-forward scoring:

TRADEABLE / CAUTION / NO-TRADE

Candidate causal domains to preregister before use include:
- deterministic calendar/session constraints such as late-Friday / weekly close and known market maintenance/holiday windows;
- scheduled macro-event windows;
- causal microstructure stress such as abnormal spread, liquidity disappearance, gaps/slippage or quote instability;
- causal shock-regime detection for extreme volatility / unscheduled geopolitical or news shocks.

Critical governance rule: these domains must be defined prospectively and cannot be retroactively applied to remove historical failures. Thresholds or event rules must be frozen before evaluation. The operability layer controls whether the strategy participates; it does not rewrite the historical predictor verdicts.

Fresh-forward Exp27 remains the decisive anti-overfitting gate before runtime promotion or any new claim of generalization.

## 2026-08-14 18:12 BRT — Decision Layer 01 frozen: STRUCTURAL EDGE / GEOMETRY BREAK-EVEN

This is a downstream decision-layer experiment, NOT Exp54 and NOT a reopening of historical timing-feature discovery. It adds no market feature and does not alter Exp27. Historical Validation/Test are repeatedly inspected and remain exploratory; this experiment can establish historical structural/economic coherence only, never runtime promotion.

### Scientific question

Does the already-frozen Exp47 minimal factorized corridor law translate into a stable economic expectancy when the model probability of the exit side is compared with the break-even probability implied by the current corridor geometry?

The key identity is derived without fitting a new parameter.

For a current structural state let:

```text
B = oriented distance from current close to BACK boundary
F = oriented distance from current close to FORWARD boundary
W = B + F
P = CorridorPosition = B / W
```

For horizon H, reuse only the frozen Exp47 components:

```text
e(H) = P(EXIT by H) from the elapsed-time BASE survival clock
q(H) = P(ADVANCE | EXIT by H, Position) from the frozen POSITION side law
```

The Exp47 factorization is:

```text
P(ADVANCE by H) = e(H) * q(H)
P(RECAPTURE by H) = e(H) * (1-q(H))
P(NO_EXIT by H) = 1-e(H)
```

For an ADVANCE-side corridor-resolution payoff of +F on ADVANCE, -B on RECAPTURE and 0 on NO_EXIT:

```text
EV_ADV(H)
= e(H) * [q(H)*F - (1-q(H))*B]
= e(H) * W * [q(H) - P]
```

Therefore the frozen probability edge is:

```text
EDGE_PROB(H) = q(H) - CorridorPosition
```

and the scale-normalized structural expectancy is:

```text
STRUCTURAL_EDGE_ATR(H)
= e(H) * CorridorWidthATR * EDGE_PROB(H)
```

This is an algebraic consequence of the already-frozen probability law plus the already-observed corridor geometry. No coefficient, threshold, bucket, interaction or new feature is fitted.

### Frozen realized payoff target

Use the exact Exp47 eligible state-horizon cells at H = 15/30/60/120 minutes and the exact first-passage labels/censoring already used by Exp47.

At each eligible state-horizon cell, distances are frozen at state_time and normalized by the same causal state ATR:

```text
B_ATR = B / ATR_state
F_ATR = F / ATR_state
```

Define the ADVANCE-side realized corridor-resolution payoff:

```text
Y_ADV_ATR(H) =
    +F_ATR   if ADVANCE occurs first by H
    -B_ATR   if RECAPTURE occurs first by H
     0       if NO_EXIT by H
```

Censored cells remain excluded exactly as in Exp47. No mark-to-market value is invented for censored cells.

The zero-threshold policy is frozen before score:

```text
if EDGE_PROB(H) > 0: choose ADVANCE
if EDGE_PROB(H) < 0: choose RECAPTURE
if EDGE_PROB(H) = 0: WAIT
```

The corresponding realized policy payoff is:

```text
Y_POLICY_ATR(H) = sign(EDGE_PROB(H)) * Y_ADV_ATR(H)
```

and predicted policy expectancy is:

```text
PRED_POLICY_EV_ATR(H) = abs(STRUCTURAL_EDGE_ATR(H))
```

No minimum edge threshold is allowed in DL01.

### Frozen evaluation universe

Reuse the exact Exp47 historical OOS universe:
- same dynamic states and exact guards;
- same eligible horizons 15/30/60/120;
- same eight joint Direction x Time environments from Exp44/45/47;
- same historical cutoff < 2026-08-13 00:00:00 BRT;
- no fresh-forward Exp27 row;
- no retrospective OPERABILITY01 filtering.

In particular, do NOT remove Friday close, scheduled-news periods, high-volatility rows, outliers or any historically adverse environment. Operability remains a separate prospective participation layer.

### Primary estimand and dependence control

Primary estimand = STATE_HORIZON_WEIGHTED within each frozen environment, matching Exp47. Dependence-aware inference = whole-BRT-day bootstrap preserving all state-horizon cells from each sampled day and computing total statistic / total sampled cells.

Two primary formal tests are frozen per environment:

A) EXPECTANCY CALIBRATION VALUE

Compare continuous predicted `STRUCTURAL_EDGE_ATR` against the realized `Y_ADV_ATR` using squared-error gain over a zero-EV baseline:

```text
MSE_GAIN = MSE(0, Y_ADV_ATR) - MSE(STRUCTURAL_EDGE_ATR, Y_ADV_ATR)
```

Positive means the factorized structural expectancy estimates realized corridor payoff better than assuming zero expectancy everywhere.

B) ZERO-THRESHOLD POLICY PAYOFF

```text
MEAN_POLICY_PAYOFF_ATR = mean(Y_POLICY_ATR)
```

Positive means the sign of the structural edge selects the higher-value corridor side on average without tuning a threshold.

Formal historical PASS requires, in all eight environments:
- MSE_GAIN point estimate > 0 and whole-day bootstrap CI95 lower bound > 0; AND
- MEAN_POLICY_PAYOFF_ATR point estimate > 0 and whole-day bootstrap CI95 lower bound > 0.

Thus the universal formal gate is 16/16 cells. Any environment failing either criterion means `ROBUST_STRUCTURAL_DECISION_EDGE = FAIL` under DL01.

### Frozen diagnostics only

Report without rescue authority:
- results by individual horizon 15/30/60/120;
- mean/median `EDGE_PROB`, `abs(EDGE_PROB)` and predicted structural EV;
- ADVANCE/RECAPTURE policy-side fractions and exact-zero WAIT fraction;
- Spearman/Pearson association between predicted `STRUCTURAL_EDGE_ATR` and `Y_ADV_ATR`;
- realized payoff conditional on observed ADVANCE/RECAPTURE/NO_EXIT;
- probability-sum and algebraic identity errors;
- coverage, days and class counts per environment.

Diagnostics cannot create thresholds, slices or interactions after score.

### Explicitly excluded from DL01

DL01 is a structural gross-expectancy test, not a deployable trading backtest. Therefore it deliberately excludes:
- spread;
- slippage;
- commission;
- financing/swap;
- order latency;
- fill uncertainty;
- position sizing;
- stop/TP engineering outside the fixed corridor boundaries;
- overlapping-position portfolio accounting;
- OPERABILITY01 historical filtering.

If DL01 passes, the next separately frozen Decision Layer experiment may add realistic execution costs and a non-overlapping execution policy. Costs may reduce or eliminate the edge; they cannot be tuned to rescue DL01.

### Anti-rescue / governance

After DL01 is scored:
- no `EDGE > x` threshold search;
- no top-decile/top-quartile edge subset;
- no horizon deletion;
- no environment deletion;
- no direction-specific recalibration;
- no day/session/news/Friday exclusion;
- no alternate payoff after seeing results;
- no new feature or refit;
- no use of Exp27 fresh-forward data;
- no runtime promotion.

Failure rejects the universal historical decision-edge claim but does not erase Exp47 probability-law PASS. Success establishes only historical gross structural expectancy and still requires fresh-forward validation plus costs/execution before any runtime trading claim.

